---
description: QuotePilot core project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

QuotePilot is a quote-first SaaS for residential electricians (V1). Follow SPEC.md
and build phase by phase (SPEC §14). Implement only the requested phase.

Stack: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript, Tailwind + shadcn/ui, Supabase (Postgres +
Auth), Drizzle ORM, OpenAI SDK, Resend, Paddle, Vercel.

Golden rules:

- Mobile-first always; the user is on a phone at a job site.
- TypeScript strict; no `any` without a reason.
- All external calls (OpenAI, Resend, Paddle, Supabase admin) go through /lib
  wrappers. No raw external calls in components.
- Secrets, AI, email, billing run server-side only. Never expose secret keys.
- Multi-tenant: every query scoped by business_id + protected by RLS.
- Money is integer cents, never floats.
- AI never sets an unmatched price; pricebook is source of truth; owner reviews
  every quote before sending.
- Always record quote_events (viewed/accepted/etc.) — the data moat.
- Validate AI output against the schema; retry once then graceful error.
- Every screen handles loading, empty, and error states.
- Small functions, boring libraries. Commit after each phase.
